    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d320">

                <pb facs="0357" n="241" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg241"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1352b.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-29T20:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 29, 1914, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Please explain to the Minister for Foreign Affairs that the action taken by the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Machias</hi> should not be regarded as indicative of
                    any hostility towards the Bordas Government much less of favor to the
                    revolutionists, but that it was considered by this Government as a step
                    necessary for the protection of non-combatants in Puerto Plata.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
